        {
            "content_html": "<img src=\"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/195330143?v=4\" width=\"64\" height=\"64\" alt=\"\"/><br/>\n<h4 dir=\"auto\">Summary</h4>\n<p dir=\"auto\">Added a note under Firefox support for <code class=\"notranslate\">ClipboardEvent.clipboardData</code> indicating that when pasting multiple files, Firefox only returns the first file. This is based on bug <a href=\"https://bugzil.la/1954680\" rel=\"nofollow\">1954680</a>.</p>\n<h4 dir=\"auto\">Test results and supporting details</h4>\n<p dir=\"auto\">Tested locally using <code class=\"notranslate\">npm test</code> in mdn/browser-compat-data. All tests pass successfully.</p>\n<h4 dir=\"auto\">Related issues</h4>\n<p dir=\"auto\"><span class=\"issue-keyword tooltipped tooltipped-se\" aria-label=\"This pull request closes issue #27687.\">Fixes</span> <a class=\"issue-link js-issue-link\" data-error-text=\"Failed to load title\" data-id=\"3359104520\" data-permission-text=\"Title is private\" data-url=\"https://github.com/mdn/browser-compat-data/issues/27687\" data-hovercard-type=\"issue\" data-hovercard-url=\"/mdn/browser-compat-data/issues/27687/hovercard\" href=\"https://github.com/mdn/browser-compat-data/issues/27687\">#27687</a></p>\n",
            "url": "https://github.com/mdn/browser-compat-data/pull/27713",
            "title": "Add Firefox clipboardData note about only pasting first file",
            "date_modified": "2025-08-30T09:11:01.000Z",
            "date_published": "2025-08-30T09:10:25.000Z",
            "author": {
                "name": "ZunedKhan07",
                "url": "https://github.com/ZunedKhan07"
            }
        },
        {
            "content_html": "<img src=\"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/47647?u=2fbfc431a85d357f00c0146d5e55b425b7f00a3d&v=4\" width=\"64\" height=\"64\" alt=\"\"/><br/>\n<h4 dir=\"auto\">Summary</h4>\n<p dir=\"auto\">Chrome 139 adds support for 3D textures using BC and ASTC compressed formats. See <a href=\"https://chromestatus.com/feature/5080855386783744\" rel=\"nofollow\">https://chromestatus.com/feature/5080855386783744</a>, and also see <a href=\"https://developer.chrome.com/blog/new-in-webgpu-139#3d_texture_support_for_bc_and_astc_compressed_formats\" rel=\"nofollow\">https://developer.chrome.com/blog/new-in-webgpu-139#3d_texture_support_for_bc_and_astc_compressed_formats</a> for a bit more explanation.</p>\n<p dir=\"auto\">This PR adds a data point for the WebGPU <code class=\"notranslate\">GPUSupportedFeatures</code> required to enable these texture usages.</p>\n\n<h4 dir=\"auto\">Test results and supporting details</h4>\n\n\n<h4 dir=\"auto\">Related issues</h4>\n\n",
            "url": "https://github.com/mdn/browser-compat-data/pull/27709",
            "title": "Chrome 139 WebGPU 3D compressed texture features",
            "date_modified": "2025-08-29T11:26:38.000Z",
            "date_published": "2025-08-29T11:26:03.000Z",
            "author": {
                "name": "chrisdavidmills",
                "url": "https://github.com/chrisdavidmills"
            }
        },
        {
            "content_html": "<img src=\"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/349114?u=1185d4fc45f5ff4c4a592b30a4dd2bb5cd1b7128&v=4\" width=\"64\" height=\"64\" alt=\"\"/><br/><p dir=\"auto\">This is a bit of a test PR to see if we could add spec_urls everywhere (especially for behavioral sub features).<br>\nSome things came up where we should probably agree on spec_url consistency for a few common sub features:</p>\n<ul dir=\"auto\">\n<li>worker_support</li>\n<li>iterable sub features (forEach, keys, values, iterator, etc)</li>\n<li>secure_context_required<br>\nI decided to use the spec_url for the interface itself, happy to hear other thoughts.</li>\n</ul>\n<p dir=\"auto\">Also, I think when a sub aspect of e.g. a method is described then it is okay to link to the same spec section as the method. So, basically the sub feature gets the same spec_url as the parent feature.</p>\n<p dir=\"auto\">I marked standard_track false for a few things: CSSPrimitiveValue, CSSValue, CSSValueList. Doesn't look like these will be going anywhere.</p>",
            "url": "https://github.com/mdn/browser-compat-data/pull/27671",
            "title": "Add more spec_urls; set some standard_tracks to false (APIs A-C)",
            "date_modified": "2025-08-29T18:33:39.000Z",
            "date_published": "2025-08-26T13:10:28.000Z",
            "author": {
                "name": "Elchi3",
                "url": "https://github.com/Elchi3"
            }
        },
        {
            "content_html": "<img src=\"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/7352080?v=4\" width=\"64\" height=\"64\" alt=\"\"/><br/><h4 dir=\"auto\">Summary</h4>\n<p dir=\"auto\">Add to the browser compatibility data for <code class=\"notranslate\">browserSetting.verticalTabs</code> introduced by <a href=\"https://bugzilla.mozilla.org/show_bug.cgi?id=1946600\" rel=\"nofollow\">Bug 1946600</a> Add a new browserSetting property that determines whether vertical tabs are enabled.</p>\n<h4 dir=\"auto\">Related issues</h4>\n<p dir=\"auto\">Related MDN content changes in TBC</p>",
            "url": "https://github.com/mdn/browser-compat-data/pull/27657",
            "title": "Bug-1946600 addition of webextension.api.browserSetting.verticalTabs",
